# Repository Rules

- Develop the maintained desktop application in `app_electron/`; keep new behavior out of the Python fallback unless explicitly requested.
- Keep renderer, preload, and main-process responsibilities separate. Renderer code must use the narrow `window.artistApp` API and must not import Node or Electron APIs.
- Preserve the JSON data contract and relative image paths. Validate every filesystem path in the Electron main process and keep destructive file operations inside the managed `images/` directory.
- Never add local user data, reference images, secrets, `node_modules`, Electron binaries, or generated release folders to Git.
- Keep list work virtualized and lazy so the number of rendered cards stays tied to the viewport.
- Update architecture and setup documentation when changing storage, startup, or module boundaries.
